# Innocent Blood on turn 3 with two creatures on each side: "Each player sacrifices a creature of their choice." The caster
# is a player too, so Bot1 chooses first (as the active player, CR 101.4) and sacrifices its own Ornithopter, not the Llanowar
# Elves it cast first, keeping the Elves; Bot2 chooses its Ornithopter, keeping the Elves. Each side loses exactly one creature and the spell
# itself ends in its owner's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Swamp
Ornithopter
Innocent Blood
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Innocent Blood.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Swamp; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Graveyard = Innocent Blood; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
